  "summary": "Created a new page, Study · Problems typing shortcuts, with six editable 1493 × 1033 encounter screens and retained local menu compositions. Uses the existing Maya encounter shell, linked DS Menu/Item focus/disabled states, DS problem chips, DS tokens, Akkurat content, and published Elevation / 8.",
  "verified": [
    "All six final screen states inspected in the composition screenshot",
    "Active-problem picker inspected at native desktop resolution",
    "Nine linked menu/chip controls match their actual masters structurally and by tokens",
    "All 25 measured assertions pass, including menu bounds, screen widths, caret presence, authored typography and entity-chip counts",
    "No image-filled nodes in the screen board; UI consists of editable layers and linked instances"
  ],
  "findings": [
    "Initial build return exceeded the 48 KB tool limit and was rolled back; page inventory confirmed no changes before retry. Retry reports authored roots and retains inherited descendants via those roots.",
    "Horizontal gallery rows were changed to hug their screen heights. Published Elevation / 8 replaces the initial local shadow.",
    "Insertion carets are editable 1 × 24 rectangles placed after typed commands or the final inserted chip.",
    "Initial chip-count assertion included nested icon instances; corrected to count the five explicitly created chip roots. Final assertion results pass.",
    "Pre-existing Nav/Search placeholder typography uses Inter in the source and all six copied encounter shells. Retained as DS-governed content; new authored note and menu content uses Akkurat LL.",
    "These are visual screen states; typing and keyboard behavior are described, not implemented or played through as an interactive prototype.",
    "The empty state reuses Maya’s encounter shell as a scenario fixture. It does not change actual patient data."
  ],
